    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.k_edge_components - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.k_edge_components.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.k_edge_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find the k-edge-connected components of a graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.k_edge_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find the k-edge-connected components of a graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.k_edge_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find the k-edge-connected components of a graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind the k-edge-connected components of a graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L70951-L71048){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.k_edge_components(k)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![k-edge-connected components](../assets/graphs/k-edge-components.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Two triangles joined by the bridge C–D. With k = 2, nodes belong together when two edge-disjoint paths join them: the triangle A, B, C (accent region) and the triangle D, E, F (teal region) qualify, while the faded bridge offers only one path between them. The card lists the two components; with k = 3 all 6 nodes are separate.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nTwo nodes belong to the same k-edge-connected component when at least `k` edges must be\nremoved to separate them, that is, when they are joined by `k` edge-disjoint paths in the\nwhole graph. These classes partition the nodes: with `k=1` they are the connected\ncomponents, with `k=2` the pieces left after removing the bridges, and larger `k` finds\never more robustly linked groups, as in finding the parts of a communication or\ntransport network that survive any `k - 1` link failures.\n\nThe paths may pass through nodes outside the component, so a component need not induce a\nk-edge-connected subgraph by itself; use `k_edge_subgraphs()` for that stricter notion.\nOn a directed graph, paths follow edge direction and two nodes belong together when `k`\nedge-disjoint paths run each way between them; with `k=1` the components are the\nstrongly connected components. Parallel edges count separately and self-loops are\nignored.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[k]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The required number of edge-disjoint paths (at least 1).\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The components as sorted lists of node IDs (every node appears in exactly one;\n    nodes in no larger group form singletons).\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `k` is less than 1.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nOn undirected graphs, the method builds a Gomory-Hu tree with unit edge capacities\n(Gusfield's algorithm, $V - 1$ maximum flows with Dinic's algorithm). The local edge\nconnectivity of two nodes is the smallest weight on their tree path, so removing the tree\nedges lighter than `k` leaves exactly the components. Directed graphs have no Gomory-Hu\ntree, but the relation \"`k` edge-disjoint paths both ways\" is still transitive, so each\ncomponent is found as the nodes mutually k-edge-connected to its first remaining node,\ntwo maximum flows per node and component. NetworkX's `k_edge_components` gives the same\npartition, except that it returns nothing for a single-node undirected graph when `k` is\n3 or more.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~k_edge_subgraphs`) \n\n:   Groups that are k-edge-connected using only their own edges.\n\n[](`~k_components`) \n\n:   The node-connectivity counterpart.\n\n[](`~bridges`) \n\n:   The edges between the 2-edge-connected components.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn two triangles joined by a bridge, `k=2` separates the triangles, and `k=3` separates\nevery node, since a triangle only offers two edge-disjoint paths between its corners:\n\n::: {#c342c8be .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [\n        (\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\"), (\"C\", \"D\"),\n        (\"D\", \"E\"), (\"E\", \"F\"), (\"F\", \"D\"),\n    ]\n)\n\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\n(\n    [[label(n) for n in c] for c in graph.k_edge_components(2)],\n    len(graph.k_edge_components(3)),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n([['A', 'B', 'C'], ['D', 'E', 'F']], 6)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The most robustly linked stations\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. Six stations around the city center are\njoined to each other by three routes that share no stretch of track, so no two\nclosures can separate them. Every other station is in a group of its own:\n\n::: {#5016e47e .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\ngroups = metro.k_edge_components(3)\n\n[[metro.get_label_from_id(n) for n in g] for g in groups if len(g) > 1]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[['Old Town', 'Central', 'Market', 'Northpark', 'Museum', 'Riverside']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#4f542a33 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsix = max(groups, key=len)\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", highlight=six, label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark